STATIC HTML VS PRESENTATION
===========================

HTML should primarily describe:

STRUCTURE
+
MEANING


CSS should primarily control:

APPEARANCE
+
LAYOUT


Avoid using semantic elements merely to create visual spacing.

Examples to avoid:

empty <p> elements for spacing

repeated <br> elements for layout

tables for general page layout


NATIVE HTML FIRST
=================

One of the most important rules from the entire HTML curriculum:

USE THE NATIVE ELEMENT THAT MATCHES THE JOB.


Need a button?

<button>


Need navigation?

<nav>


Need a hyperlink?

<a>


Need an input label?

<label>


Need a table?

<table>


Need a heading?

<h1> through <h6>


Need a list?

<ul> or <ol>


Need primary content?

<main>


Only reach for additional ARIA when native HTML does not already
communicate the required information.


FINAL HTML CHECKLIST
====================

Before considering an HTML page complete, check:

DOCUMENT

- DOCTYPE exists
- lang is set
- charset is UTF-8
- viewport metadata exists
- useful title exists
- useful description exists


STRUCTURE

- semantic elements used appropriately
- one clear main content area
- headings form a logical hierarchy
- no unnecessary generic containers


LINKS

- destinations are correct
- internal href fragments match IDs
- link text is meaningful


IMAGES

- every image has appropriate alt handling
- informative images have useful descriptions
- decorative images use empty alt text


FORMS

- controls have labels
- for/id relationships match
- names exist where data must be submitted
- appropriate input types are used
- validation attributes match requirements
- radio buttons are properly grouped
- checkboxes have meaningful values
- help text is properly associated when necessary


TABLES

- used only for tabular data
- caption describes the table
- table sections are appropriate
- header cells use correct semantics
- row/column relationships are clear


ARIA

- native HTML used first
- ARIA is actually necessary
- referenced IDs exist
- accessible names are meaningful
- aria-hidden does not remove important information


MEDIA

- native controls are available
- video captions are provided when necessary
- audio transcripts are available
- fallback text exists where appropriate


KEYBOARD

- all interactive controls are reachable
- tab order is logical
- static text is not an unnecessary tab stop
- positive tabindex values are avoided


VALIDATION

- HTML validator passes
- accessibility audit performed
- keyboard testing performed
- DevTools inspection performed


